cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the paper (preferred-citation); if you use the stablerun model, also cite the software."
title: "stablerun: agent-based stress test of stablecoin runs and Treasury-bill fire-sale spillovers"
abstract: >-
  Calibrated agent-based model of a payment-stablecoin run: heterogeneous
  holders, a secondary market with capital-constrained arbitrage, an issuer
  with a redemption queue and a liquidation waterfall, and a Treasury-bill
  market with permanent and temporary price impact. Calibrated to the USDC
  (March 2023) and USDT (May 2022) episodes, with experiments on spillover
  size, the systemic tipping point, policy levers, contagion and sensitivity.
type: software
